CLASS net/minecraft/class_1_5 net/minecraft/world/LightUtil
	COMMENT Contains helper methods for manipulating lightmap coordinates.
	COMMENT <p>
	COMMENT Lightmap coordinates are stored as two 16-bit integers packed in an {@code int}.
	COMMENT The lower 16 bits store the block light level, while the upper 16 bits store
	COMMENT the sky light level. Only the lower 8 bits of each component are used; the
	COMMENT upper 8 bits are always set to zero. Since the lightmap texture is 16×16,
	COMMENT this allows for a resolution of 1/16 of a texel on each axis.
	COMMENT <p>
	COMMENT The methods suffixed with {@code 44} deal with block and sky light levels
	COMMENT expressed as “4.4” fixed point, where bits 4 to 7 describe the integral
	COMMENT light level and bits 0 to 3 correspond to the fractional part. The
	COMMENT corresponding methods without the {@code 44} suffix take or return the
	COMMENT integral parts of these, setting the fractional part to zero or ignoring
	COMMENT them.
	FIELD field_1_24 FULL I
	FIELD field_1_25 SKY I
	FIELD field_1_26 MAX_COMPONENT I
	METHOD method_1_386 increaseBlockLight (IF)I
		ARG 0 packed
		ARG 1 fraction
	METHOD method_1_387 getBlock (I)I
		ARG 0 packed
	METHOD method_1_388 addEmission (II)I
		ARG 0 light
		ARG 1 emission
	METHOD method_1_389 max (II)I
		ARG 0 light1
		ARG 1 light2
	METHOD method_1_390 pack (II)I
		ARG 0 block
		ARG 1 sky
	METHOD method_1_391 getSky (I)I
		ARG 0 packed
	METHOD method_1_392 blend (IIII)I
		COMMENT This method is used in the ambient occlusion algorithm.
		ARG 0 neighbor1
		ARG 1 neighbor2
		ARG 2 neighbor3
		ARG 3 central
	METHOD method_1_393 getBlock44 (I)I
		ARG 0 packed
	METHOD method_1_394 pack44 (II)I
		ARG 0 block44
		ARG 1 sky44
	METHOD method_1_395 getSky44 (I)I
		ARG 0 packed
	METHOD method_1_396 weightedAverage (IIIIFFFF)I
		ARG 0 a
